# Data Analytics — Complete Summary Notes

# 1. Data

## Definition

Data means raw facts and figures collected from different sources.

Examples:

* Marks = 90
* Temperature = 42°C
* Student names
* Images and videos

---

# 2. Types of Data

## (A) Structured Data

Fixed format me organized data.

### Examples

* Excel sheets
* Database tables
* Bank records

### Diagram

```text
+---------+--------+-------+
| Roll No | Name   | Marks |
+---------+--------+-------+
| 101     | Adit   | 90    |
| 102     | Rahul  | 85    |
+---------+--------+-------+
```

### Features

* Easy to search
* Rows and columns format
* Fast analysis

---

## (B) Unstructured Data

Jiska koi fixed format nahi hota.

### Examples

* Videos
* Images
* Emails
* Social media posts

### Diagram

```text
Image   Video   Audio   Text
  *       *       *      *
```

### Features

* Difficult to analyze
* Huge amount of data

---

## (C) Semi-Structured Data

Partially organized data.

### Examples

* JSON
* XML
* HTML

### Example JSON

```json
{
  "name": "Adit",
  "marks": 90
}
```

### Features

* Flexible structure
* Easier than unstructured data

---

# 3. DIKW Model

## Data → Information → Knowledge → Wisdom

```text
           Wisdom
        (Decision Making)

           Knowledge
       (Understanding)

          Information
      (Processed Data)

              Data
         (Raw Facts)
```

---

## Example

### Data

```text
85, 90, 78
```

### Information

```text
Average marks = 84.3
```

### Knowledge

```text
Student performance is good.
```

### Wisdom

```text
Student should get scholarship.
```

